# Generated third-party (KICS) corpus (rebuilt by build_foreign_corpus.py from a
# pinned KICS checkout). The mapping (kics_mapping.py) and builder are tracked;
# the imported fixtures are not. The scored evidence (metrics.json, report,
# tables) is committed under evaluation/results/foreign/ instead.
evaluation/dataset/foreign/

# ===================================
# Track B Stage 0 — fuzzing baseline (run fuzz-baseline-20260721-213507)
# ===================================
# The raw crash corpus is ~72 MB of near-duplicate libFuzzer artifacts: 18,983
# files that the triage gate collapses to 24 stack signatures and 6 confirmed
# bugs. The scored evidence (baseline.json, baseline_report.md, the run log) and
# the MINIMISED reproducers are the load-bearing parts and stay tracked — a
# 2-byte deterministic reproducer is the reproducibility gate's whole point.
# Everything else is re-derivable by re-running scripts/gcp_fuzz_baseline.sh.
evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/artifacts/**
!evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/artifacts/
!evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/artifacts/*/
!evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/artifacts/**/min-*
evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/corpus/
evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/live/

# ===================================
# A.3 threshold calibration (canonical run ml-calib-20260721-215119)
# ===================================
# per_config_scores.csv.gz + training_reference_scores.csv.gz ARE tracked on
# purpose: they make every future threshold re-derivable offline with zero paid
# compute, which is the entire hedge against the GCP credits expiring 2026-07-22.
# The heartbeat mirror, the multi-MB run log, the intermediate stage-1 dump and
# the corpus manifests are not — they are provenance, not evidence.
evaluation/results/ml_calibration/live/
evaluation/results/ml_calibration/home/
evaluation/results/ml_calibration/manifests/
evaluation/results/ml_calibration/tv-calib.log
evaluation/results/ml_calibration/collect_*.txt
# The superseded first pass is kept on disk as an independent replicate, but only
# its metrics and report are worth versioning (see ml_calibration/RUNS.md).
evaluation/results/ml_calibration_run1_superseded/**
!evaluation/results/ml_calibration_run1_superseded/
!evaluation/results/ml_calibration_run1_superseded/ml_calibration_metrics.json
!evaluation/results/ml_calibration_run1_superseded/report_ml_calibration.md

# The fuzzing run log is the ONLY place executed_units / execs-per-second can be
# recovered from (libFuzzer fork mode exits before -print_final_stats). Force-tracked
# against the global *.log rule above — see fuzz_baseline/BASELINE_CORRECTIONS.md.
!evaluation/results/fuzz_baseline/tv-fuzz.log
